-- Bitemporal stamps (smucclaw/l4-ide#914 §2A): every ledger append carries a
-- transaction time (at=, the ROOT eval clock) and, when a fact time was
-- explicitly in scope at the write, a valid-from (vt=). The rendered Ledger
-- blocks below lock three invariants:
--
--   * a plain RECORD is contemporaneous: at= the harness clock, NO vt= field;
--   * a RECORD under EVAL UNDER VALID TIME carries vt=<the asserted day>;
--   * tx-IMMUNITY (the audit invariant): a RECORD under EVAL AS OF SYSTEM
--     TIME STILL stamps at= the harness clock, not the override — that
--     clause scopes reads, never writes.
--
-- Harness clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z.

-- expected: 1 — and a Ledger row [source=RECORD, at=2025-01-31T15:45:30Z] with no vt=
#EVAL RECORD `a` IS 1

-- expected: 2 — and a Ledger row with vt=2020-01-01
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020)) (RECORD `b` IS 2)

-- expected: 3 — and a Ledger row with at=2025-01-31T15:45:30Z (NOT 2020) and no vt=
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020)) (RECORD `c` IS 3)
